      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Triad",
      "body": "The most common chord is the **triad**: a note, the note a 3rd above it, and the note a 3rd above that. On the white keys that is every other key: C E G, or D F A.\n\n**Why it matters:** Almost every chord on a band chart is a triad or is built from one. Learn the triad and you can play most songs.",
